{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Which one slaughters outside the camp</b> — The pericope of slaughtering outside is juxtaposed to the scapegoat, to teach you: even though I permitted to you the scapegoat outside by pushing it off the cliff (צוק), and the meaning of צוק is rocks that have protruding tooth-like points, and this is its slaughter — even so, take care with other consecrated offerings not to slaughter them outside."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:36.293549188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}